From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] terminal: the Terminal app opens a shell on the device

NickelOS has a real terminal: opening the Terminal app starts a login
shell of the signed-in user on the device. The connections page (SSH,
settings) stays pinned as the first tab.

- guest_os::LaunchTerminalDefault(): opening the Terminal app (the web
  app publisher's Terminal launch) opens "vmshell" for the NickelOS host
  (VM "nickel", container "host"); without host apps it is
  LaunchTerminalHome() as before. Other LaunchTerminalHome() callers
  (the Files app's SFTP mount flow) are unchanged.
- terminalPrivate: vmshell for the host runs nickel-terminal-shell
  locally instead of vsh into a VM: nickel-appd starts a login shell of
  the session user in their home directory, outside the no_new_privs and
  Landlock sandbox session_manager puts Chrome in, so sudo and mount work.
  Arguments after `--` (Terminal=true apps) run in that shell instead of a
  prompt.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/guest_os/guest_os_terminal.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/guest_os/guest_os_terminal.cc
index b0a134935ca3b..1f80964ab6170 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/guest_os/guest_os_terminal.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/guest_os/guest_os_terminal.cc
@@ -208,6 +208,19 @@ void LaunchTerminalHome(Profile* profile, int64_t display_id, int restore_id) {
                         GURL(GetTerminalHomeUrl()));
 }
 
+void LaunchTerminalDefault(Profile* profile,
+                           int64_t display_id,
+                           int restore_id) {
+  if (!crostini::IsNickelNativeAppsAllowed(profile)) {
+    return LaunchTerminalHome(profile, display_id, restore_id);
+  }
+  LaunchTerminalWithUrl(
+      profile, display_id, restore_id,
+      GenerateTerminalURL(profile, /*settings_profile=*/std::string(),
+                          GuestId(VmType::TERMINA, crostini::kNickelVmName,
+                                  crostini::kNickelContainerName)));
+}
+
 void LaunchTerminalWithUrl(Profile* profile,
                            int64_t display_id,
                            int restore_id,
